text:
Quality score: **6/10**. The code is small, readable, and has a decent focused test suite, but I would not approve it as-is because the ingest/upsert path can silently preserve stale accounting data or overwrite newer terminal data. That is core correctness for this tool.

I ran `python -m pytest -q`: **61 passed**. I also reproduced the two main ingest bugs manually with in-memory SQLite. Estimated rewrite/significant-change scope: **about 140 lines**, mostly in `db.py`, parser validation, report timestamp handling, CLI error handling, and new regression tests.

```json
{
  "score": 6,
  "issues": [
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "70-80",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Upsert treats a record as unchanged when only user, partition, submit, start, alloc_cpus, gpus, or exit_code changed, leaving stale accounting data."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "71-84",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Same-rank terminal states overwrite each other without comparing freshness, so an older FAILED/TIMEOUT/etc. snapshot can replace a newer terminal record."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "110-114, 148-163",
      "severity": "high",
      "description": "Negative AllocCPUS and gres/gpu values are accepted and can produce negative CPU/GPU-hour reports."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "118-126",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Timezone-aware timestamps are accepted without normalization even though downstream storage and reporting assume comparable timestamp text."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "14, 65, 83, 101, 115, 142",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Report filters and MAX compare timestamps lexicographically, which gives wrong results for offset-aware or mixed-format ISO timestamps."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
      "lines": "52-58",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "The default database directory and file are created with normal umask permissions, commonly 0755/0644, exposing local job/user data on shared systems."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "121-180",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Report commands call db.connect and silently create a new empty database for a mistyped path instead of failing clearly."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/reports.py",
      "lines": "124-148",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Top users includes zero-GPU pending jobs and can anchor the trailing window on a pending submit time, hiding actual recent GPU usage."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/cli.py",
      "lines": "99-117",
      "severity": "medium",
      "description": "Ingest commits well-formed rows before returning a fatal malformed-row exit code, leaving a nonzero command with persistent partial side effects."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/parser.py",
      "lines": "73-75",
      "severity": "low",
      "description": "Step detection skips any JobID containing a dot instead of validating Slurm step syntax, risking accidental loss of valid non-step IDs."
    },
    {
      "file": "jobwatch/db.py",
